#!/bin/sh
# The graft × crate matrix: three shapes that only a real host with a real cargo can answer, each of
# which was hand-measured before it was written down here.
# graft × crate 位置矩阵：三种只有"真宿主 + 真 cargo"能回答的形状，每一种都是先手工量过才写进这里。
#
#   1. a cut on the **root face** with `full` — the whole tree replaced from the top;
#   2. **overlapping** cuts (one inside another) — must be refused **by name**, not silently applied;
#   3. a **re-partition** of the host (the subtree holding both cuts handed to a new crate) — the plan
#      must not change and every crate must still build;
#   4. the **replacement's own subtree** — `ControlFast` declares two children of its own, and a `full` cut
#      replaces the subtree at **runtime**: none of them may enter the host's generated tree;
#   5. **middle nodes** — a non-`full` cut, a range over faces that have children, and `full` on a middle
#      node: all three publish the **same** faces, because what a build publishes is decided by the subtrees
#      the cuts name and `full` only decides how deep the runtime replacement goes.
#   6. **two identical string cuts** for one slot — named as an overlap with a winner, and **not** fatal: the
#      hand-off list recorded this as a defect and it measured false, so this leg asserts the opposite.
#   7. **moving a face a graft names** — the move must refuse with a `determined` repair map before writing
#      anything; after unmounting that entry the same move applies, and the host still `check`s and builds.
#   1. 切口落在**根面**上并带 `full`——整棵树从顶被替换；
#   2. **重叠**的两条切口（一条在另一条里面）——必须**点名拒绝**，不许静默生效；
#   3. 把宿主**重新划分**（装着两条切口的那棵子树交给新 crate）——计划不得改变，各 crate 仍要能构建；
#   4. **替换方自己的子树**——`ControlFast` 自己也声明了两个子面，而 `full` 切口替换的是**运行期**的子树：
#      它们一个都不许进入宿主的生成树；
#   5. **中间节点**——非 `full` 的切口、覆盖"有子面的面"的区间、以及落在中间节点上的 `full`：三者发布
#      **同一批**面，因为一次构建发布哪些面由切口点名的**子树**决定，而 `full` 只决定运行期替换覆盖多深。
#   6. 同一槽位的**两条相同字符串切口**——被点名为重叠并给出赢家，而且**不致命**：交接清单把它记成缺陷，
#      实测不成立，因此这条腿断言的是它的反面。
#   7. **移动一个被 graft 点名的面**——移动必须在写盘前拒绝并给出 `determined` 修复映射；卸下那条条目之后
#      同一次移动可以落地，宿主仍然 `check` 通过并能构建。
#
# **Repaired 2026-10-18 — this gate runs green again, and the repair found a product defect.**
# What was wrong: the legs rewrote the host's `GRAFTS` with regexes against the **old** `cut(...) graft(...)` spelling;
# the example migrated to the `graft(...).with(...)` builder, so every rewrite silently matched nothing and the shape
# under test was the unmodified host. On top of that, `host()` copied only `host/` + `graft/` while the example is
# partitioned into `crates/` ghosts, so the host's generated tree lacked the catalog faces the legs graft.
# Now: `host()` copies the whole example, `set_grafts` rewrites the declaration wholesale (and **fails** when it
# cannot), legs 2/4/5/6 use **string** selectors (a typed cut on a delegated subtree stops the host publishing that
# subtree's catalog constants), and leg 3/6 run on `host_unpartitioned` because their premise is a host that has not
# been split. **The repair also found a real defect**: two cuts naming one slot left the plan with **no row** (the drop
# was keyed by subtree, so the winner went with the loser) — fixed in `pipeline.rs` with the pin
# `two_cuts_for_one_slot_leave_exactly_the_winners_row`.
# **2026-10-18 已修复——这道门禁重新变绿，而这次修复抓到了一个产品缺陷。**
# 原来错在两处：各腿用正则改宿主的 `GRAFTS`，改的是**旧**拼法 `cut(...) graft(...)`；示例已迁到
# `graft(...).with(...)` 构建器，于是每次改写都静默不匹配，被测形状其实是没被改过的宿主。此外 `host()` 只复制
# `host/` + `graft/`，而示例已被划分进 `crates/` 幽灵，所以宿主的生成树缺少各腿要 graft 的 catalog 面。
# 现在：`host()` 复制整个示例；`set_grafts` 整块改写声明（改不了就**失败**）；leg 2/4/5/6 用**字符串**选择器
# （类型化切口落在被交出的子树上会让宿主不再发布那棵子树的 catalog 常量）；leg 3/6 跑在 `host_unpartitioned` 上，
# 因为它们的前提是还没被拆分过的宿主。**这次修复还抓到一个真缺陷**：两条切口点名同一个槽位会让计划**一行都不剩**
# （丢弃按子树作键，赢家跟着输家一起没了）——已在 `pipeline.rs` 修掉，钉子是
# `two_cuts_for_one_slot_leave_exactly_the_winners_row`。
#
# Usage: tools/xirang-graft-matrix        (XIRANG_GRAFT_MATRIX_CARGO_FLAGS to override)
# 用法：tools/xirang-graft-matrix        （用 XIRANG_GRAFT_MATRIX_CARGO_FLAGS 覆盖 cargo 旗标）
set -u
ROOT=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
WORK=$(mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/xirang-graft-matrix.XXXXXX")
CARGO_FLAGS="${XIRANG_GRAFT_MATRIX_CARGO_FLAGS---offline}"
XIRANG="$ROOT/target/debug/xirang"
# Build the binary this script drives, rather than assuming somebody else did: a fresh checkout has no
# `target/debug/xirang`, and a gate that only passes where it was built by hand fails on the machine
# that matters (measured on CI). Self-contained on purpose — this runs before the helpers below exist.
# 自己构建本脚本要驱动的二进制：全新检出不带它，而在"有人手工构建过"的机器上才通过的闸门，恰好在最要紧的
# 那台机器上失败（CI 实测）。这里刻意不依赖下面的辅助函数——它跑在它们定义之前。
if [ ! -x "$XIRANG" ]; then
  echo "building the CLI this matrix drives" >&2
  "${CARGO:-cargo}" build ${CARGO_FLAGS-} -p xirang-toolchain --features cli --bin xirang >&2 ||
    { echo "cannot build $XIRANG" >&2; exit 1; }
fi
fail() { printf 'graft matrix FAILED: %s\n' "$1" >&2; exit 1; }
step() { printf '== %s\n' "$1"; }
build() { command cargo build $CARGO_FLAGS "$@"; }

step "building the CLI this matrix drives"
build -p xirang-toolchain --features cli --bin xirang >/dev/null 2>&1 ||
  fail "cannot build $XIRANG"

host() {
  area="$WORK/$1"
  mkdir -p "$area"
  # The **whole** example, not two of its three parts. `crates/` holds the ghosts the shipped host was partitioned
  # into, and the host's build script reads that shape: with the ghosts missing it generates a different tree whose
  # catalog no longer carries the faces these legs graft. Measured 2026-10-18 — copying only `host/` + `graft/` made
  # leg 2 die with `error[E0425]: cannot find value BUTTON in module crate::catalog::control::object`, which read
  # like a product defect for two rounds.
  # **整个**示例，而不是它的三分之二。`crates/` 装着出厂宿主被划分出来的幽灵，而宿主的构建脚本读的就是那个形状：
  # 缺了幽灵它会生成另一棵 catalog 不再携带这些面要 graft 的东西的树。2026-10-18 实测——只复制 `host/` 与
  # `graft/` 会让 leg 2 死在 `error[E0425]: cannot find value BUTTON in module crate::catalog::control::object`，
  # 而那读起来像产品缺陷，骗了两轮。
  cp -a "$ROOT/examples/partitioned-button/host" "$area/app"
  cp -a "$ROOT/examples/partitioned-button/graft" "$area/ext"
  cp -a "$ROOT/examples/partitioned-button/crates" "$area/crates"
  printf '[workspace]\nresolver = "3"\nmembers = ["app", "ext", "crates/partitioned-button-objects", "crates/partitioned-button-facade"]\n' >"$area/Cargo.toml"
  for manifest in "$area/app/Cargo.toml" "$area/ext/Cargo.toml" \
    "$area/crates/partitioned-button-objects/Cargo.toml" "$area/crates/partitioned-button-facade/Cargo.toml"; do
    [ -f "$manifest" ] || continue
    sed -i "s#path = \"../../../../toolchain\"#path = \"$ROOT/toolchain\"#g; s#path = \"../../../toolchain\"#path = \"$ROOT/toolchain\"#g" "$manifest"
    sed -i 's#path = "\.\./\.\./graft"#path = "../../ext"#g; s#path = "\.\./graft"#path = "../ext"#g' "$manifest"
    sed -i 's#path = "\.\./\.\./host"#path = "../../app"#g; s#path = "\.\./host"#path = "../app"#g' "$manifest"
  done
  echo "$area"
}

# A host **before** the split: the example's own sources and its graft provider, without the ghosts and without the
# declaration that already partitioned it. Leg 3 asks "does re-partitioning change the plan", so it needs the tree on
# the near side of a partition; every other leg runs on the shipped (partitioned) copy.
# **划分之前**的宿主：示例自己的源码与它的 graft 提供方，不带幽灵、也不带那条已经把它划分掉的声明。leg 3 问的是
# "重新划分会不会改变计划"，所以它需要划分**之前**那一边的树；其余各腿跑在出厂（已划分）副本上。
host_unpartitioned() {
  area="$WORK/$1"
  mkdir -p "$area"
  cp -a "$ROOT/examples/partitioned-button/host" "$area/app"
  cp -a "$ROOT/examples/partitioned-button/graft" "$area/ext"
  rm -f "$area/app/add_crates.rs"
  printf '[workspace]\nresolver = "3"\nmembers = ["app", "ext"]\n' >"$area/Cargo.toml"
  sed -i "s#path = \"../../../toolchain\"#path = \"$ROOT/toolchain\"#g" "$area/app/Cargo.toml" "$area/ext/Cargo.toml"
  sed -i 's#path = "\.\./graft"#path = "../ext"#' "$area/app/Cargo.toml"
  echo "$area"
}

# Rewrite the host's `GRAFTS` declaration wholesale, from a list of expressions.
# 按一份表达式清单整块重写宿主的 `GRAFTS` 声明。
#
# The legs below used to substitute the *old* `cut(...) graft(...)` spelling with regexes, and when the example
# migrated to the `graft(...).with(...)` builder every one of those regexes silently stopped matching: the shape
# under test was then the **unmodified** host, and the failure read as "the root-face cut does not check" (measured
# 2026-10-18 on a clean HEAD copy). An edit that must happen has to **fail** when it cannot.
# 下面几条腿过去用正则替换**旧的** `cut(...) graft(...)` 拼法；示例迁到 `graft(...).with(...)` 之后，那些正则
# 全部静默失配：被测形状其实是**没被改过**的宿主，失败读起来像"根面切口 check 不过"（2026-10-18 在干净的 HEAD
# 副本上实测）。**必须发生的**编辑，做不了就得**失败**。
set_grafts() {
  python3 - "$@" <<'REWRITE'
import pathlib, sys

path = pathlib.Path(sys.argv[1])
entries = sys.argv[2:]
text = path.read_text()
marker = "pub const GRAFTS: &[Graft] = &["
start = text.index(marker)
end = text.index("];", start)
body = "\n".join(f"    {entry}," for entry in entries)
path.write_text(text[:start] + marker + "\n" + body + "\n" + text[end:])
print(f"grafts: {len(entries)}")
REWRITE
}

step 'leg 1/7: a cut on the root face with full'
AREA=$(host root-cut)
set_grafts "$AREA/app/src/lib.rs" \
  'graft(subtree(crate::ROOT_NODE_ID)).with(control_button_graft::control_fast::NODE_ID)' ||
  fail "the host's graft declaration could not be rewritten"
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the root-face cut does not check"
[ "$(sed -n '2p' "$AREA/app/target/xirang/out/graft_plan.tsv" | cut -f1)" = "crate::ROOT_NODE_ID" ] ||
  fail "the plan does not record the root-face cut"
(cd "$AREA/app" && build >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the root-face cut does not build"

step "leg 2/7: overlapping cuts keep the later entry and say which one answers"
AREA=$(host overlap)
# **String** selectors, and that is not a shortcut: this example is partitioned, so `control` and everything under it
# belongs to a ghost crate, and a declaration that takes `control` as a cut target stops publishing its catalog
# constants from the host — the typed spelling then does not compile (`error[E0425]: cannot find value BUTTON`, measured
# 2026-10-18). Strings are addressed by logical path instead, which survives the partition, and they exercise the same
# overlap rule.
# **字符串**选择器，而不是走捷径：这个示例已被划分，`control` 及其下的一切属于幽灵 crate，而一条把 `control` 当
# 切口目标的声明会让宿主不再发布它的 catalog 常量——类型化拼法于是编译不过（2026-10-18 实测
# `error[E0425]: cannot find value BUTTON`）。字符串按逻辑路径寻址，能穿过划分，而且走的是同一条重叠规则。
set_grafts "$AREA/app/src/lib.rs" \
  'graft("root/control/button").with("button_fast")' \
  'graft(subtree("root/control")).with("control_fast")' \
  'graft("root/control/slider").with("slider_fast")' ||
  fail "the host's graft declaration could not be rewritten"
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >"$WORK/overlap.out" 2>&1) ||
  fail "overlapping cuts no longer check: $(head -3 "$WORK/overlap.out")"
# The decision is spoken: both entries named, and which one answers.
grep -q "two graft cuts overlap" "$WORK/overlap.out" ||
  fail "the overlap went unmentioned: $(head -3 "$WORK/overlap.out")"
grep -q "later, wins" "$WORK/overlap.out" ||
  fail "the hint does not say which entry answers: $(grep -m1 overlap "$WORK/overlap.out")"
printf '   hint: %s\n' "$(grep -m1 'two graft cuts overlap' "$WORK/overlap.out" | cut -c1-200)"
# And only the winner reaches the plan: the later `control` full entry replaces the earlier button cut.
#
# Read through the **facade** shape, because this fixture's host has handed `control` — and everything under
# it, including the slider — to a ghost: a host that no longer compiles the cut face legitimately emits no cut
# for it, and reading the host's own table here looked exactly like a missing plan. That is the same mistake
# the other two device criteria made (audit `M7`, §M7.55), and it is worth spelling out: the shape-independent
# witness to "which cut won" is the crate that carries the union.
# 经 **facade** 形状读，因为这个夹具的宿主已经把 `control`——以及它之下的一切，包括 slider——交给了一个幽灵：
# 一个不再编译那个切口面的宿主合法地不为它发射切口，而在这里读宿主自己的表，看起来与"计划缺失"一模一样。这与
# 另外两处装置判据犯的是同一个错误（审计 `M7`，§M7.55），值得写明：**"哪条切口赢了"**这个问题的与形状无关的
# 证人，是那个携带并集的 crate。
XIRANG_SHAPE_FACADE=1 "$XIRANG" check "$AREA/app" >/dev/null 2>&1 ||
  fail "the facade shape does not check"
PLAN="$AREA/app/target/xirang/out/graft_plan.tsv"
[ -f "$PLAN" ] || fail "no graft plan to read"
# The fixture declares three cuts — `button`, then `control` (full), then `slider`. Pairwise "later
# wins" therefore leaves exactly the **last** one: `slider` supersedes `control`, which superseded
# `button`. Both earlier entries must be gone from the plan, and the last one must be in it.
# 夹具声明了三条切口——`button`、`control`(full)、`slider`。逐对"后者赢"因此只留下**最后**一条：
# `slider` 盖住 `control`，`control` 又盖住 `button`。前两条都必须从计划里消失，最后一条必须在。
# The plan prints each selector in the **module-path** spelling, whatever the declaration wrote: a declaration
# may name `crate::catalog::control::object::SLIDER`, and the plan then says
# `crate::control::object::slider::NODE_ID` (measured 2026-10-18). Both spellings name the same face; the plan's
# own normalisation is what these lines read.
# 计划把每个选择器印成**模块路径**拼法，与声明里怎么写无关：声明可以写
# `crate::catalog::control::object::SLIDER`，而计划说 `crate::control::object::slider::NODE_ID`（2026-10-18 实测）。
# 两种拼法指的是同一个面；这几行读的是计划自己的归一化。
# The plan prints a string selector as the **logical path** it names (`root/control/slider`), so the rows are compared
# field by field rather than by substring: `root/control` is a prefix of every path under it, and a substring test would
# read the winner as three rows.
# 计划把字符串选择器印成它点名的**逻辑路径**（`root/control/slider`），因此逐字段比较而不是子串比较：`root/control`
# 是它下面每条路径的前缀，用子串会把这个赢家读成三行。
cut_rows=$(awk -F'\t' 'NR > 1 && NF { print $1 }' "$PLAN")
printf '%s\n' "$cut_rows" | grep -qx "root/control/slider" ||
  fail "the last cut is not in the plan: $(printf '%s ' $cut_rows)"
if printf '%s\n' "$cut_rows" | grep -qx "root/control/button"; then
  fail "a superseded cut is still in the plan"
fi
if printf '%s\n' "$cut_rows" | grep -qx "root/control"; then
  fail "the intermediate cut is still in the plan"
fi
(cd "$AREA/app" && build >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the overlapping host does not build"

step "leg 3/7: re-partitioning the host keeps the plan and every crate"
# The **unpartitioned** copy: this leg's premise is a host that has not been split yet, and the shipped example has
# already been. Running it on the shipped copy would overwrite a declaration whose ghosts are still workspace members
# and then build two partitions of one host at once — measured 2026-10-18: `a crate of the split does not build`.
# **未划分**的副本：这条腿的前提是一棵还没被拆分过的宿主，而出厂示例已经拆过了。跑在出厂副本上会覆盖一条声明、
# 而它的幽灵仍是工作区成员，于是一次构建一个宿主的两份划分——2026-10-18 实测：`a crate of the split does not build`。
AREA=$(host_unpartitioned repartition)
cat >"$AREA/app/add_crates.rs" <<'RS'
use xirang_toolchain::run_method::{Crate, Shape};

pub fn add_crates() -> Shape {
    Shape::of("app", &[Crate::named("objects").at(&[crate::control::SUBTREE])])
}
RS
# The plan to compare against is the one the **declaration** publishes, so it is taken *after* the first
# `check` — not before it. Read before, this line hashed whatever happened to sit in the copied
# `host/target/`: on a machine that had built the example it is the same plan and the comparison passes,
# and on a fresh checkout (CI) the file is absent, so `md5sum` hashed empty input and every run failed
# with "re-partitioning changed the graft plan". Measured — that is exactly how this leg failed on CI
# while passing locally. The existence check below is what keeps a missing plan from comparing two
# empty hashes and reporting success.
# 用来比较的那份计划是**声明**发布出来的，因此在第一次 `check` **之后**取，而不是之前。在它之前读，这一行
# 哈希的是复制过来的 `host/target/` 里恰好躺着的东西：在构建过示例的机器上它就是同一份计划，于是比较通过；
# 而在全新检出（CI）上该文件不存在，`md5sum` 哈希的是空输入，于是每次都报 "re-partitioning changed the
# graft plan"。实测——这正是这条腿在 CI 上红而本地绿的原因。下面的存在性检查正是让"计划缺失"不会变成
# "两个空哈希相等、于是报成功"。
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the declared host does not check"
# The witness is the **facade shape's own** table, read before and after the split. Not the host's: this
# fixture declares a crate, so the host has handed that subtree away and legitimately emits fewer cuts than the
# declaration names — reading the host here is the mistake this file has now made three times (audit `M7`,
# §M7.55). The facade carries the union, so its plan is the shape-independent reading of "what does this tree
# declare", and asking for it twice is exactly the question this leg exists to ask: does re-partitioning change
# it?
# 证人是 **facade 形状自己**的表，在拆分前后各读一次。不是宿主的：这个夹具声明了一个 crate，因此宿主已经把
# 那棵子树交出去、合法地少发几条——在这里读宿主，就是本文件已经犯过三次的那个错误（审计 `M7`，§M7.55）。
# facade 携带并集，因此它的计划是"这棵树声明了什么"的与形状无关的读法，而问它两次正是这条腿存在的意义：
# 重新划分会不会改变它？
facade_plan() {
  XIRANG_SHAPE_FACADE=1 "$XIRANG" check "$AREA/app" >/dev/null 2>&1 ||
    fail "the facade shape does not check"
  cat "$AREA/app/target/xirang/out/graft_plan.tsv"
}
before=$(facade_plan)
[ -n "$(printf '%s' "$before" | tail -n +2)" ] ||
  fail "the facade carries no cut at all, so this leg would compare two empty plans: $before"
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" crates --write . >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the split is not written"
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the split host does not check"
# The partition root is the **workspace** root, so the generated packages sit beside the host, and the
# remap config it wrote is found by running cargo from there.
# 划分根是**工作区**根：生成包落在宿主旁边，而它写下的 remap 配置要靠"从那里跑 cargo"才会被找到。
[ -d "$AREA/crates/app-objects" ] || fail "the split did not produce the ghost"
[ -d "$AREA/crates/app-facade" ] || fail "the split did not produce the facade"
(cd "$AREA" && build --workspace >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "a crate of the split does not build"
after=$(facade_plan)
[ "$before" = "$after" ] ||
  fail "re-partitioning changed the cuts the tree declares (the facade's plan moved)"
cuts=$(find "$AREA/target" "$AREA/crates" -path "*app-objects-*/out/generated_lib.rs" 2>/dev/null | head -1)
[ -n "$cuts" ] || fail "no generated tree for the ghost"
[ "$(grep -c 'StaticGraftCut::from_ids' "$cuts")" = "2" ] ||
  fail "the ghost does not emit both cuts"

step 'leg 4/7: the replacement never brings its own subtree in'
AREA=$(host replacement-subtree)
set_grafts "$AREA/app/src/lib.rs" \
  'graft(subtree(crate::catalog::control::NODE_ID)).with(control_button_graft::control_fast::NODE_ID)' ||
  fail "the host's graft declaration could not be rewritten"
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the replacing cut does not check"
(cd "$AREA/app" && build >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the replacing cut does not build"
TREE=$(ls -t "$AREA"/target/debug/build/*/out/generated_lib.rs 2>/dev/null | head -1)
[ -n "$TREE" ] || fail "no generated tree to read"
# The replacement declares three faces of its own — `ControlFast` and two children — and a `full` cut replaces
# the subtree **at runtime**. None of those faces may enter the host's generated tree: the host compiles what it
# compiles, and the replacement's subtree belongs to the replacement's crate (audit `M7`, §M7.65).
# 替换方自己也声明了三个面——`ControlFast` 与两个子面——而 `full` 切口替换的是**运行期**的子树。那些面一个都
# 不许进入宿主的生成树：宿主编译它编译的那些，而替换方的子树属于替换方那个 crate（审计 `M7`，§M7.65）。
for kind in ControlFast ButtonFast SliderFast; do
  [ "$(grep -c "$kind" "$TREE")" = "0" ] ||
    fail "the replacement's own face $kind entered the host's generated tree"
done
printf '   the replacement declares 3 faces of its own; none entered the host tree\n'

step 'leg 5/7: middle nodes — non-full, a range over faces with children, and full'
# Three shapes whose answer is the **same**, and it has been read wrong twice: which faces a build publishes is
# decided by the subtrees the cuts **name**, and `full` only decides how deep the **runtime** replacement goes
# (audit `M7`, §M7.56/§M7.65). Each is judged on the `slots` of `explain --overlay`, which a separate
# measurement showed to agree with the generated tree.
# 三种形状的答案是**同一个**，而它被读错过两次：一次构建发布哪些面由切口点名的**子树**决定，而 `full` 只决定
# **运行期**替换覆盖多深（审计 `M7`，§M7.56/§M7.65）。每一种都用 `explain --overlay` 的 slots 判定，而
# 另一次实测表明它与生成树一致。
for shape in middle-nonfull range-with-children middle-full; do
  AREA=$(host "$shape")
  case "$shape" in
    middle-nonfull)
      set_grafts "$AREA/app/src/lib.rs" \
        'graft(crate::catalog::control::NODE_ID).with(control_button_graft::control_fast::NODE_ID)' ||
        fail "the $shape declaration could not be rewritten"
      ;;
    range-with-children)
      set_grafts "$AREA/app/src/lib.rs" \
        'graft(range(crate::catalog::control::object::BUTTON, crate::catalog::control::object::SLIDER)).with(control_button_graft::button_fast::NODE_ID)' ||
        fail "the $shape declaration could not be rewritten"
      ;;
    middle-full)
      set_grafts "$AREA/app/src/lib.rs" \
        'graft(subtree(crate::catalog::control::NODE_ID)).with(control_button_graft::control_fast::NODE_ID)' ||
        fail "the $shape declaration could not be rewritten"
      ;;
  esac
  (cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >/dev/null 2>&1) || fail "the $shape shape does not check"
  SLOTS=$("$XIRANG" explain --overlay --path "$AREA/app" 2>/dev/null)
  # Logical paths, not module paths: a face at `control/object/button/button.rs` has the module path
  # `control::object::button` and the **logical** path `root/control/button` — the overlay prints the latter,
  # and asserting the former is how this leg's first version failed (audit `M7`, §M7.65).
  # 逻辑路径，不是模块路径：住在 `control/object/button/button.rs` 的面，模块路径是 `control::object::button`，
  # 而**逻辑**路径是 `root/control/button`——overlay 印的是后者，而断言前者正是这条腿第一版失败的原因
  # （审计 `M7`，§M7.65）。
  for face in root/control root/control/button root/control/slider; do
    printf '%s' "$SLOTS" | grep -q "$face" ||
      fail "the $shape shape does not publish $face — a cut names subtrees, and full does not prune the build"
  done
  printf '   %s: control and both of its children are published\n' "$shape"
done

step 'leg 6/7: two identical string cuts for one slot'
# The unpartitioned copy, because this leg reads the plan of the **host** and a string cut on `root/control/button`
# is only the host's to emit while it still publishes that subtree: in the shipped copy `control` belongs to a ghost,
# and the host's plan legitimately carries no row for it (measured 2026-10-18: `0 row(s)`).
# **未划分**的副本，因为这条腿读的是**宿主**的计划，而 `root/control/button` 的字符串切口只有在宿主还发布那棵子树时
# 才由它发射：在出厂副本里 `control` 属于幽灵，宿主的计划合法地不带这一行（2026-10-18 实测：`0 row(s)`）。
AREA=$(host_unpartitioned identical-cuts)
set_grafts "$AREA/app/src/lib.rs" \
  'graft("root/control/button").with("button_fast")' \
  'graft("root/control/button").with("button_fast")' ||
  fail "the host's graft declaration could not be rewritten"
# The hand-off list recorded this shape as a defect — "two identical string cuts make the build fail with a
# reason that contradicts the file" — and it measured false. This leg is what keeps that answer honest: it
# asserts the **opposite** of the claim, so a change that ever makes the claim true fails here.
# 交接清单把这个形状记成缺陷——"同一槽位两条相同的字符串切口会让构建失败，且理由与文件矛盾"——而它实测不成立。
# 这条腿就是让那个答案保持诚实的东西：它断言的是那句话的**反面**，因此哪天那句话成真，这里会红。
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >"$WORK/identical.out" 2>&1) ||
  fail "two identical string cuts do not check: $(head -3 "$WORK/identical.out")"
grep -q "two graft cuts overlap" "$WORK/identical.out" ||
  fail "the overlap went unmentioned: $(head -3 "$WORK/identical.out")"
grep -q "later, wins" "$WORK/identical.out" ||
  fail "the hint does not say which entry answers"
ROWS=$(printf '%s' "$(cat "$AREA/app/target/xirang/out/graft_plan.tsv")" | tail -n +2 | grep -c . || true)
[ "$ROWS" = "1" ] ||
  fail "the plan does not carry exactly the winning cut ($ROWS row(s)): $(facade_plan | tr '\n' ' ')"
(cd "$AREA/app" && build >/dev/null 2>&1) ||
  fail "the build fails on two identical string cuts (the hand-off list said it would; it does not)"
printf '   identical cuts: check ok, the overlap is named, one row survives, and the build succeeds\n'


step 'leg 7/7: moving a face a graft names, then repairing and moving it'
# The plan-level pins already cover the four graft/move interactions this leg exercises with a **real build**:
# `an_ancestor_move_checks_typed_and_string_grafts_on_descendants`, `moving_out_of_a_full_graft_cannot_silently_restore_the_base_object`,
# `recorded_grafts_on_only_some_moved_objects_are_named_before_writing`, `rebinding_only_the_moved_record_restores_both_external_implementations`
# and `cross_crate_moves_report_ownership_without_changing_claims_or_unrelated_grafts`. What none of them proves is
# that the **product path** refuses, the repair is possible, and the host still builds — this leg asks exactly that.
# 计划层已经有四条 graft/move 交互的钉子；它们都不证明**产品路径**会拒绝、修复可完成、宿主仍能构建，这条腿问的就是这三件事。
MCP="$ROOT/target/debug/xirang-mcp"
if [ ! -x "$MCP" ]; then
  (cd "$ROOT" && cargo build $CARGO_FLAGS -p xirang-toolchain --features mcp --bin xirang-mcp >/dev/null 2>&1) ||
    fail "could not build $MCP, so the move path cannot be exercised"
fi
AREA=$(host move-repair)
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >/dev/null 2>&1 && build >/dev/null 2>&1) ||
  fail "the move-repair host does not build before anything moves"
FACE="$AREA/app/src/control/object/button/button.rs"
BEFORE=$(md5sum "$FACE" | cut -d' ' -f1)
if (cd "$AREA/app" && "$MCP" --call xirang.apply --root . --json '{"action":"move","node":"root/control/button","to":"root","apply":true}' >"$WORK/move-target.out" 2>&1); then
  fail "moving a face a graft names was applied without the repair the declaration needs"
fi
grep -q "\[determined\]" "$WORK/move-target.out" ||
  fail "the refusal does not tag the impact as determined: $(head -3 "$WORK/move-target.out")"
grep -q "No automatic repair has been applied" "$WORK/move-target.out" ||
  fail "the refusal does not say that nothing was repaired automatically"
grep -q "root/control/button -> root/button" "$WORK/move-target.out" ||
  fail "the repair map does not name the destination the move would produce"
AFTER=$(md5sum "$FACE" | cut -d' ' -f1)
[ "$BEFORE" = "$AFTER" ] ||
  fail "the refused move changed the face's bytes ($BEFORE -> $AFTER)"
# The repair the refusal asks for is possible: unmount that one entry, then move. Leaving `slider` typed is exactly
# how the shipped declaration spells the remaining entry, so the rewrite is the same shape the host already uses.
# 拒绝要求的那步修复是可行的：卸下这一条，再移动。`slider` 保留类型化拼法——出厂声明就是这么写的，所以改写后的形状与宿主现有的一致。
set_grafts "$AREA/app/src/lib.rs" \
  'graft(crate::catalog::control::object::SLIDER).with(control_button_graft::slider_fast::NODE_ID)' ||
  fail "the host's graft declaration could not be reduced to the entry that is not moving"
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >"$WORK/move-repaired-check.out" 2>&1) ||
  fail "the host does not check after the entry naming the moving face is unmounted: $(head -3 "$WORK/move-repaired-check.out")"
if ! (cd "$AREA/app" && "$MCP" --call xirang.apply --root . --json '{"action":"move","node":"root/control/button","to":"root","apply":true}' >"$WORK/move-applied.out" 2>&1); then
  fail "the same move still refuses after the repair: $(head -5 "$WORK/move-applied.out")"
fi
[ -f "$AREA/app/src/button/button.rs" ] ||
  fail "the moved face is not at src/button/button.rs after the move"
[ ! -f "$FACE" ] ||
  fail "the face is still at its old path after the move"
(cd "$AREA/app" && "$XIRANG" check . >/dev/null 2>&1) ||
  fail "the host does not check after the repaired move"
(cd "$AREA/app" && build >/dev/null 2>&1) ||
  fail "the host does not build after the repaired move"
printf '   move-repair: refused with a determined map, bytes untouched, then applied after the repair, and the host still builds\n'

printf '\nOK — seven shapes: the root-face cut builds; overlapping cuts keep the later entry with a hint; a re-partitioned host keeps its plan; the replacement subtree stays out; the three middle-node shapes publish the same faces; two identical string cuts are named rather than fatal; and a move of a graft-named face refuses with a determined map, then applies after the repair and still builds\n'
rm -rf "$WORK"
